### 5. Game Screen – Core Loop

**Day Phase Screen:**
- Top: Phase indicator “DAY” with timer (e.g., 04:59).
- Middle:
  - Event log panel (system messages, eliminations).
  - Chat panel (scrollable, day chat).
- Bottom:
  - Action bar:
    - “Vote” button (opens vote modal).
    - “View Roles” (shows your own role card only).
- Visual style: brighter than night but still dark; warm ambient light.

**Vote Modal (Day):**
- List of living players with avatars.
- Each has a “Vote” button.
- Optional: “Skip Vote” toggle if allowed.
- Confirm dialog: “Vote for [Name]? This cannot be undone this round.”

**Night Phase Screen:**
- Top: Phase indicator “NIGHT” with timer (e.g., 01:59).
- Background: darker, subtle animation (fog, flicker).
- Center:  
  - Message: “You are asleep…” for civilians.  
  - For special roles: action UI.
- For Mafia:
  - Private channel tab: “Mafia Chat”.
  - List of living players; select target to kill.
  - Confirm: “Eliminate [Name]?”
- For Doctor:
  - “Protect” button → list of players → choose target.
- For Police:
  - “Investigate” button → list → choose target.
- Event log shows only allowed info (e.g., “Night has begun”, “A player died last night” – not who).

**Role Card (Hidden Info):**
- Modal or dedicated screen:
  - Your role: e.g., “Mafia”, “Doctor”, “Civilian”.
  - Your objective (short text).
  - Special ability description.
- Only visible to that player.

